      "evidence": "template/scripts/requirement_retrospective.py `_merged_quick_prs` runs `gh pr view ... --json state` and compares the result to \"MERGED\". Any merged PR in any repository passes. There is no check of the target repository, of a `Requirement #N` reference in the PR, or of the merge commit. The receipt stores only the `owner/repo#N` strings. The retrospective's claim that the receipt \"says what was reviewed\" (design.md) therefore rests on operator assertion. This is acceptable if intended, but it should be stated in design.md.",
      "id": "quick-pr-not-bound-to-requirement",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "Quick PRs are only checked for MERGED state. Nothing ties them to the Requirement, and the receipt records no merge commit or head."
